{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #1100: declared status 'open'. Formalized: no. If $1=d_1<\\cdots<d_{\\tau(n)}=n$ are the divisors of $n$, then let $\\tau_\\perp(n)$ count the number of $i$ for which $(d_i,d_{i+1})=1$.\n\nIs it true that $\\tau_\\perp(n)/\\omega(n)\\to \\infty$ for almost all $n$? Is it true that\\[\\tau_\\perp(n)< \\exp((\\log n)^{o(1)})\\]for all $n$?\n\nLet\\[g(k) = \\max_{\\omega(n)=k}\\tau_\\perp(n),\\]where $\\omega(n)$ counts the number of distinct prime divisors of $n$, and $n$ is restricted to squarefree integers. Determine the growth of $g(k)$. Prize: no. OEIS: A325864. Tags: divisors, number theory."},"claim_id":"vcl_471ad5822389dfde904f1efe461e303053c75ec72930430d0237fc60f0a3b6dc","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:1100","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_1e44975b197f6a9b","object_root":"sha256:83606a0ab58162dcce7195fe1ddfbfea1688109edf4b6c0c6cd59c7bda4f13e5","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record"